"Alias and Unit-Aware Lookups

ExamplePROPWithUnits$(ρ_1; MATERIAL_A; P_DENSITY; 25°C)
ExamplePROPWithUnits$(ρ_2; material_b; DENSITY; 25°C)
ExamplePROPWithUnits$(ρ_3; MAT_A; RHO; 25°C)

"Bounds-Policy Reporting

ShowExamplePROP$(MATERIAL_A; P_CP; 75°C; DB_LINEAR; DB_STRICT)
ShowExamplePROP$(MATERIAL_A; P_DENSITY; 120°C; DB_LINEAR; DB_STRICT)
ShowExamplePROP$(MATERIAL_A; P_DENSITY; 120°C; DB_LINEAR; DB_CLAMP)
ShowExamplePROP$(MATERIAL_A; P_DENSITY; 120°C; DB_LINEAR; DB_EXTRAPOLATE)
ShowExamplePROP$(MATERIAL_B; P_VISCOSITY; 40°C; DB_LINEAR; DB_STRICT)

"Conclusions

'The same template API exposes the lookup value and its data-quality status so a consuming worksheet can distinguish valid interpolation from rejected, clamped, or extrapolated requests.
